SHA1: 67e67375bc371c2cf3ccf78d418b6373389de456
SHA256: 3a72ae18903eb39ae13bac5437d767f87e3aaed8f14a62e04ee05094558deaaf
Section: Utilities
Priority: optional
Description: Live process inspector for roothide
 Inspector samples every process on the device once a second and shows what the system is really doing.
 .
 ### Process list
 .
 - CPU share, memory footprint, thread count, PID, and owning user, refreshed every second
 - Search by name or PID; sort by CPU, memory, PID, or name
 - Filter down to system (root), user (mobile), or app processes
 - Pause live updates to hold a moment still
 .
 ### Per-process detail
 .
 - Resource use: CPU time, memory footprint, resident and virtual size, disk and network I/O
 - Executable path, arguments, sandbox status, and app bundle metadata
 - Separate screens for threads, open files and sockets, Mach ports, and loaded modules — each with its own search, sort order, and share action
 - Export the complete detail set as a property list for later analysis
 - Ask a process to quit (SIGTERM), or force quit it (SIGKILL)
 .
 ### Command line
 .
 `cocoainspector` answers the same queries for scripting — `list`, `inspect`, `details`, `watch`, `signal`, and `self-test` — served by `cocoainspectord`, an on-demand LaunchDaemon that holds one session at a time.
 .
 Localized into English, Simplified Chinese, Japanese, Russian, German, French, Spanish, and Arabic.
Author: OwnGoal Studio <not-gonna-reply@owngoal.dev>
Name: Inspector


